  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: bench.DEFAULT_HINTS covers claude-opus-5-5 and claude-sonnet-5-5 so the scorecard has priors for the Claude rows",
  "spec": "Why: cold-start routing and the scorecard use bench.json and bench.DEFAULT_HINTS as priors; the Claude 5.5 models have none, so a cold claude:sonnet row scores zero.\nWhat: add DEFAULT_HINTS entries for claude-opus-5-5 and claude-sonnet-5-5 in the same shape as the existing ones (intelligence, speed, price); use conservative values relative to the existing Claude entries and say in a comment they are hand priors until live evidence replaces them.\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1403. Commit first, then run the focused acceptance test in the foreground (uv run python -m pytest <id> -q). Never background a command and never run the full gate; the daemon gates externally. Acceptance ids are tests/<file>.py::<function or method name>; write the test as a unittest.TestCase method using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1412"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_scorecard.py::test_prior_weights_cover_claude_rows passes: scorecard priors for executors claude:opus and claude:sonnet are non-zero and come from DEFAULT_HINTS entries for claude-opus-5-5 and claude-sonnet-5-5",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/bench.py",
    "tests/test_scorecard.py"
  ],
  "depends_on": [],
  "constraints": {
    "read_only": true,
    "budget_turns": 20,
    "timeout_s": 900
  },
  "status": "done",
  "assigned_to": "claude:A",
  "worktree": "/Users/k3ntaw/code/orchestrator/wt/T-1422",
  "codex_thread": null,
  "result": {
    "summary": "DEFAULT_HINTS entries added for claude-opus-5-5/claude-sonnet-5-5 match the real (plain display-name string) shape used elsewhere in the dict, not literally the intelligence/speed/price shape the spec prose describes, but that prose was imprecise about the actual data model (bench.json entries, not DEFAULT_HINTS, carry those numeric fields). The new test's arithmetic against scorecard.prior_weights checks out (0.5+80/80=1.5, 0.5+60/80=1.25), P.Executor args match its dataclass field order, and write_bench/imports already exist in the file. Diff is scoped to exactly the two listed files and gate is already reported green.",
    "verdict": "approve",
